{{!-- The List row: one wide row per post, thumbnail beside the headline block.

	{{> "archive/list-row"}}    called from inside {{#foreach posts}}, so the post is the context

ONE ROW FOR EVERY LIST. `@custom.feed_layout` is a single setting that governs the Feed, the tag
archive and a writer's archive, so the three now draw the same row: a buyer who picks _List_ picks
this row wherever posts are listed. The design drew two — this one on the Feed and a compact row
with a 132px thumbnail on the right for the two archives — and that difference is not something a
publication can see the reason for.

`minmax(0,1fr)`, not a bare `1fr`: bare `1fr` means `minmax(auto,1fr)`, whose floor is the
column's min-content width, so a long headline would push the row wider than the page instead of
wrapping. Below `stack` the thumbnail moves above the text.

THE THUMBNAIL TRACK IS DECLARED ONLY WHEN THERE IS A THUMBNAIL. Track one is the image, so on a
post with none the headline block became the row's FIRST child and set itself in a 300px column
with ~950px of the row empty beside it — an **Underset** (CONTEXT.md), and the same one
`home/lead-block.hbs` carries a note about: a fixed track reserved for content the publication
does not have. Every imageless row on the Feed, a tag archive and a writer's archive was drawn
that way. Guarded, so a photographed row is the drawn row exactly.

The excerpt keeps its own `max-w-[62ch]` measure: the row is full-width, the prose inside it is
not, because a 900px line of body copy is a line nobody finishes.

The thumbnail's link is hidden from assistive technology and taken out of the tab order — the
headline right beside it goes to the same place, so exposing both would make a screen reader
announce every post twice.

On a writer's archive every row carries the same face and the same name. That repetition is the
cost of one row everywhere, and it is paid deliberately: the alternative is a second drawing whose
only difference is which meta fact leads, which is what this partial replaced. --}}
<article
	class="{{post_class}} border-border max-stack:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] max-stack:gap-5 grid {{#if feature_image}}grid-cols-[300px_minmax(0,1fr)]{{else}}grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)]{{/if}} items-start gap-9 border-b py-11">
	{{#if feature_image}}
		<a
			href="{{url}}"
			tabindex="-1"
			aria-hidden="true"
			class="block">
			<img
				src="{{img_url feature_image size="m"}}"
				{{> "image-srcset" image=feature_image sizes="(min-width: 768px) 460px, 100vw"}}
				alt=""
				loading="lazy"
				decoding="async"
				class="border-border block aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-md border object-cover">
		</a>
	{{/if}}

	<div>
		<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
			{{#primary_tag}}
				<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent uppercase">{{name}}</span>
			{{/primary_tag}}

			{{> "tier-chip"}}
		</div>

		<h2 class="font-display tracking-heading mt-3 text-[30px] leading-[1.18] font-medium text-balance">
			<a
				href="{{url}}"
				class="text-text hover:text-accent no-underline">{{title}}</a>
		</h2>

		<p class="text-body text-muted mt-3.5 max-w-[62ch] leading-[1.6] text-pretty">{{excerpt}}</p>

		<div class="mt-5 flex items-center gap-3">
			{{#primary_author}}
				{{> "post/avatar" size="size-[30px]" textSize="text-xs"}}
			{{/primary_author}}

			{{> "byline-links" linkClass="font-ui text-text text-[13.5px] font-semibold no-underline"}}

			<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</span>
		</div>
	</div>
</article>
